PR #1907: Rename recipe notes column + cursor pagination for saved recipes

Two small changes bundled because they touch the same table.

1. `user_recipes.notes` becomes `user_recipes.private_notes` ahead of the shared-collections work, so it is obvious in queries which field must never be exposed on shared views. Pure rename, no data change; the down migration restores the old name.
2. `GET /api/recipes/saved` moves from offset to cursor pagination. Offsets were drifting when users saved recipes while scrolling. The client already sends `cursor` from the previous page's `nextCursor`.

